      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We assessed each tool through the stages of a real trip: research, itinerary generation, refinement, and on-the-ground use. Evaluation drew on vendor documentation, published feature sets, and community consensus from frequent travelers, following the <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a>. Pricing in the AI travel category changes often and several tools monetize through booking commissions, so verify current terms on each vendor's site.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Itinerary quality (30%)</strong> — realistic pacing, geographically sensible day groupings, respect for opening hours and travel time, and how much manual fixing a generated plan needs</li>
        <li><strong>Personalization (25%)</strong> — whether the tool actually adapts to stated travel style, budget, pace, and interests instead of producing the same highlights for everyone</li>
        <li><strong>Real-time data (20%)</strong> — live flight prices, weather forecasts, and currency rates used in planning rather than after the fact</li>
        <li><strong>Collaboration &amp; flexibility (15%)</strong> — group editing, re-planning when dates or budget change, and export options</li>
        <li><strong>Cost &amp; ecosystem (10%)</strong> — free tier value and how well the tool fits an existing booking workflow</li>
      </ul>

